course: dictionary
lesson: 8384
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. Rubbing is one of these words. Look for clues in the sentence before you decide.
explain: «Rub your hands together to warm them.» Here rubbing means moving your hand against a surface again and again, pressing on it. Now try a different sentence: «She was rubbing out her mistake.» Rubbing out means removing pencil marks with a rubber, so the meaning changes with the sentence.
explain: Always use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If you swap «rubbing out» for «pressing hard», the sentence sounds wrong, so you know it means removing marks.
fact: Rubbing means moving something against a surface again and again, pressing on it.
fact: Rubbing out means removing pencil marks with a rubber or eraser.
fact: A rubbing is a picture made by putting paper on a rough surface and rubbing it with a crayon, such as a bark rubbing or a coin rubbing.
fact: In science, rubbing creates friction, and friction can make heat. «The rubbing turns the car's movement into heat» when the brake pads press on the wheels.
fact: Rubbing it in means reminding someone of a mistake they made, which can feel unkind.
exercise: Mia puts paper over a leaf and colours it with a crayon. What is the picture called? | A rubber | *A rubbing | A dead leg | A brake
exercise: «She spent ages rubbing out her mistake.» What does rubbing out mean here? | *Removing pencil marks with a rubber | Drawing a bigger picture | Pressing hard on a wall | Shaking hands
exercise: «Pressing the brake pedal pushes fluid along pipes that squeeze pads onto discs on the wheels, and the rubbing turns the car's movement into heat.» What is the rubbing in this sentence? | Turning the engine off | *The pads rubbing against the discs, which makes heat | Cleaning the windows | Makes the car go faster
test: «Rubbing your eyes can spread germs.» What can rubbing your eyes do? | Make them shine | *Spread germs | Make you taller | Make the sun come out
test: Grandad says, «Stop rubbing it in.» What does rubbing it in mean? | *Reminding someone of a mistake they made | Writing with a crayon | Giving someone a massage | Cleaning a window
exam: Which meaning fits «a coin rubbing»? | Removing pencil marks with a rubber | Moving a hand back and forth on a table | Pressing a brake pedal to slow a car | *A picture made by rubbing a crayon over paper placed on a rough surface
